  "explain_en": "The item that does not belong to the pre-work inspection is 'reporting the daily work log' (作業日報の報告). The daily work log is written and reported after the workday ends, recording the content and progress that was carried out — it cannot exist at the time before work starts. The other three items all belong to 始業前点検: checking the work procedure, checking the condition of tools and equipment, and checking machinery before operation.\n\nVocabulary:\n始業前点検（しぎょうまえ てんけん）: Pre-work inspection\n作業手順書（さぎょうてじゅんしょ）: Work procedure document\n器具（きぐ）: Tool, small equipment\n整備（せいび）: Maintenance, preparation\n作業日報（さぎょうにっぽう）: Daily work log\n報告（ほうこく）: Report, reporting",
